  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "UA_Server_delete",
    "file": "open62541/src/server/ua_server.c",
    "description": "The server teardown path calls workqueue delayed-callback cleanup twice: first via UA_Server_run_shutdown() (which calls UA_WorkQueue_cleanup), and then again inside UA_Server_delete() (also calling UA_WorkQueue_cleanup). UA_WorkQueue_manuallyProcessDelayed() frees delayed-callback nodes while iterating but does not make the queue state safe against a second cleanup pass in this lifecycle, so the second cleanup re-traverses stale/freed delayed-callback entries, causing heap-use-after-free.",
    "conditions": "In the fuzz_binary_message harness, attacker-controlled binary messages are processed and can create session-related delayed callbacks (allocated from UA_SessionManager_createSession and queued in server workQueue). The harness then unconditionally invokes UA_Server_run_shutdown(server) followed by UA_Server_delete(server). Because both paths perform workqueue cleanup, queued delayed callback objects are freed in shutdown and then accessed again during delete, triggering UAF when at least one delayed callback was queued by the input."
  },
